1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,272
First stop:

2
00:00:03,572 --> 00:00:05,617
a company the coffee shop pays

3
00:00:05,617 --> 00:00:06,980
to handle its cards.

4
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:09,770
It works for the shop, not for ZERO.

5
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:12,426
And it has no idea who he is.

6
00:00:13,276 --> 00:00:15,201
It only reads the first digits

7
00:00:15,201 --> 00:00:16,420
of the card number.

8
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,760
They say which network to ask,

9
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,368
and which bank is behind the card.

10
00:00:22,868 --> 00:00:24,692
Which raises a better question.

11
00:00:24,992 --> 00:00:27,224
Why does a coffee need a network at all?

12
00:00:28,968 --> 00:00:31,584
Because thousands of banks issue cards,

13
00:00:31,884 --> 00:00:33,948
and millions of shops take them.

14
00:00:34,098 --> 00:00:35,850
Most of them have never met.

15
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:37,952
The network is where they

16
00:00:37,952 --> 00:00:39,178
all agree to meet,

17
00:00:39,578 --> 00:00:41,306
under one set of rules.

18
00:00:41,956 --> 00:00:44,091
In the U.S., that's mostly

19
00:00:44,091 --> 00:00:45,652
Visa or Mastercard.

20
00:00:45,952 --> 00:00:48,499
In a single year, Visa alone

21
00:00:48,499 --> 00:00:51,136
handled 258 billion payments.

22
00:00:51,536 --> 00:00:54,104
That's about eight thousand every second.

23
00:00:55,504 --> 00:00:57,378
All of it runs through four

24
00:00:57,378 --> 00:00:58,696
giant data centers,

25
00:00:58,996 --> 00:01:00,340
with spare power,

26
00:01:00,590 --> 00:01:02,462
spare cooling

27
00:01:02,612 --> 00:01:04,148
and spare connections,

28
00:01:04,298 --> 00:01:06,530
so a question never has to wait.

29
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,440
Here's the strange part.

30
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:14,924
The network doesn't move money either.

31
00:01:15,124 --> 00:01:16,588
It moves questions.

32
00:01:17,988 --> 00:01:20,268
Last stop: ZERO's bank.

33
00:01:20,568 --> 00:01:22,440
The one that gave him the card.

34
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,561
It has a fraction of a second

35
00:01:24,561 --> 00:01:25,952
to answer two things.

36
00:01:26,352 --> 00:01:27,936
Does he have enough credit?

37
00:01:28,336 --> 00:01:29,704
And is this really him?

38
00:01:30,688 --> 00:01:33,472
For the second one, it doesn't ask ZERO.

39
00:01:33,772 --> 00:01:35,644
It asks his habits.

40
00:01:35,944 --> 00:01:38,788
Visa says its own system weighs more than

41
00:01:38,788 --> 00:01:41,632
five hundred details about every payment,

42
00:01:42,032 --> 00:01:43,904
in about a millisecond.

43
00:01:44,454 --> 00:01:46,662
But ZERO's card is brand new.

44
00:01:46,962 --> 00:01:48,474
He has no habits.

45
00:01:48,774 --> 00:01:50,310
And to a fraud machine,

46
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:52,319
no history can look a lot

47
00:01:52,319 --> 00:01:53,542
like a stolen card.

48
00:01:55,154 --> 00:01:57,026
Back in the coffee shop,

49
00:01:57,326 --> 00:01:59,822
the clock says one point one seconds.

50
00:02:00,372 --> 00:02:02,247
If a bank ever takes too

51
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:03,732
long, or goes down,

52
00:02:04,032 --> 00:02:05,904
the network can answer for it,

53
00:02:06,004 --> 00:02:07,876
using AI to stand in.

54
00:02:07,976 --> 00:02:10,064
But ZERO's bank isn't down.

55
00:02:10,564 --> 00:02:12,436
It's just not sure.

56
00:02:13,186 --> 00:02:15,058
Then the evidence adds up.

57
00:02:15,358 --> 00:02:16,534
A real chip,

58
00:02:16,934 --> 00:02:19,166
one only the real card can make.

59
00:02:19,266 --> 00:02:20,538
A tiny amount.

60
00:02:20,938 --> 00:02:22,607
A coffee shop a few blocks

61
00:02:22,607 --> 00:02:23,698
from his address.

62
00:02:25,286 --> 00:02:26,846
Credit: yes.

63
00:02:27,146 --> 00:02:28,539
And now look at what the

64
00:02:28,539 --> 00:02:29,642
bank actually does.

65
00:02:30,042 --> 00:02:31,866
It doesn't send any money.

66
00:02:32,166 --> 00:02:34,568
It puts a hold on four seventy-five

67
00:02:34,568 --> 00:02:36,078
of ZERO's credit line.

68
00:02:36,378 --> 00:02:38,250
A promise.

69
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:41,810
And the promise works both ways.

70
00:02:42,110 --> 00:02:43,982
If the coffee never showed up,

71
00:02:44,382 --> 00:02:46,422
ZERO could dispute the charge,

72
00:02:46,522 --> 00:02:48,059
and the money would be pulled

73
00:02:48,059 --> 00:02:49,066
back from the shop.

74
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:52,358
The answer rides back the same way.

75
00:02:52,658 --> 00:02:53,474
Bank,

76
00:02:53,774 --> 00:02:55,646
network,

77
00:02:55,846 --> 00:02:57,142
the shop's company,

78
00:02:57,342 --> 00:02:58,422
the terminal.

79
00:02:59,722 --> 00:03:01,594
Two seconds.

80
00:03:03,422 --> 00:03:05,150
ZERO thinks he just paid.

81
00:03:05,450 --> 00:03:06,386
He didn't.

82
00:03:06,886 --> 00:03:08,830
Nobody has paid anybody.

83
00:03:09,330 --> 00:03:11,202
Not yet.

84
00:03:11,502 --> 00:03:13,758
So when does the money actually move?
